// A group blessing against despair. D&D's "advantage on Wisdom saves and
// death saving throws" has no save-advantage primitive, and "healing
// received is always maximized" has no healing-multiplier primitive either
// (checked every `BuffEffect` in common/src/comp/buff.rs), so both riders
// are dropped. The closest still-fitting primitive is `Fearless`
// ("Immunity to Terrified -- a tag-only buff") -- steadfast resolve against
// fear/despair reads as a reasonable, if narrower, stand-in for "advantage
// on saves against a hopeless death". `strength: 1.0` is the same no-op
// placeholder freedom_of_movement.ron already uses for its own tag-only
// buff, since `Fearless` has no numeric effect of its own.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: Fearless,
            strength: 1.0,
            duration: Some(60.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(60.0),
    range: 9.0,
    energy_cost: 40.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Divine)),
)
